@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# Solution
+
+The cache's `get` method returned values without moving their keys to the most-recently-used end of the `OrderedDict`, so later insertions could evict a recently read entry. It now refreshes recency after a successful, non-expired lookup.
+
+The `put` method also evicted an entry whenever the cache was full, even when updating a key already present. Eviction is now performed only when inserting a new key into a full cache; updates replace the value and refresh that key's recency without removing another entry.
